    "total_tokens": 295,
    "description": "WellaPath Nigeria CDSS \u2014 Symptom Token Dictionary. Machine-readable vocabulary for all 50 pilot conditions. All tokens are lowercase_snake_case. No duplicates across categories.",
    "rules": [
      "All tokens lowercase_snake_case \u2014 no spaces, no hyphens, no capitals",
      "No duplicate tokens across the entire dictionary",
      "Common symptoms shared across conditions use the SAME token",
      "Tokens must be atomic \u2014 one concept per token",
      "Once locked, tokens cannot be renamed without a schema version bump"
    ],
    "corrections_from_v0": [
      "Added 6 missing symptom_tokens found in KB symptom_weights: abdominal_cramps, backache, difficulty_breathing, excessive_thirst, frequent_urination, wheeze",
      "Removed 'wheezing' \u2014 consolidated into 'wheeze' as canonical token (wheeze used in chronic_respiratory; wheezing was duplicate synonym)",
      "Removed duplicate 'haemoptysis' from symptom_tokens \u2014 haemoptysis is a red flag (blood in sputum = danger sign); kept only in red_flag_tokens",
      "Removed duplicate 'petechial_rash' from red_flag_tokens \u2014 petechial_rash as observed symptom stays in symptom_tokens; severe petechial rash with fever = red flag handled via condition logic",
      "Added 'petechial_rash_fever' as dedicated red_flag_token to distinguish the danger sign from the symptom observation",
      "Removed 'exertional_shortness_of_breath' \u2014 consolidated into 'exertional_breathlessness' (synonym, exertional_breathlessness already present)",
      "Kept 'hearing_loss' \u2014 valid symptom for ear_infections and chronic conditions even if not currently in symptom_weights JSON",
      "v1.1: Split severe_malnutrition_sam_mam into two tokens \u2014 severe_malnutrition_sam (escalate_emergency) and moderate_malnutrition_mam (increase_urgency). Clinical rationale: MAM and SAM have different urgency thresholds."
    ],
